 the body's tissues, which can affect nutritional status and body composition.", "MASA LIBRE DE GRASA:Lean body mass refers to the weight of everything in the body except fat, an important measure in assessing body composition.", "OBESIDAD MÓRBIDA:\"OBESIDAD MÓRBIDA,\" or morbid obesity, is a severe medical condition characterized by excessive body weight that significantly increases the risk of various health complications. This condition has been discussed in clinical cases, highlighting its impact on patients who often experience multiple attempts at weight loss and may ultimately require surgical intervention, such as bariatric surgery. Morbid obesity is resistant to conventional treatment methods and is associated with serious health issues, including diabetes and an increased risk of pancreatic cancer. Management of morbid obesity often necessitates specific nutritional strategies, particularly for critically ill patients, to address the complex health challenges it presents. Overall, morbid obesity is a critical health concern that demands comprehensive medical attention and intervention.", "RUIZ LÓPEZ:Ruiz López is a medical doctor who contributed to the work on nutrition in older adults.", "ARTACHO MARTÍN LAGOS:Artacho Martín Lagos is a researcher involved in the study of nutrition in older adults.", "QUILES MORALES:Quiles Morales is a researcher who co-authored the work on nutrition in older adults.", "NUTRICIÓN EN EL ADULTO MAYOR:A chapter in a book discussing nutrition specifically for older adults.", "LATHAM:Latham is a researcher who authored works on human nutrition in developing countries, contributing to the understanding of malnutrition.", "ALIMENTACIÓN Y NUTRICIÓN:A collection by FAO that discusses food and nutrition, focusing on global issues related to hunger and malnutrition.", "GONZALO MARÍN M:Gonzalo Marín M is an author who has contributed to research in clinical nutrition and metabolism. He has also collaborated on works related to nutritional requirements and diet therapy. His contributions reflect a focus on understanding the complexities of nutrition and its application in clinical settings.", "DIETOTERAPIA, NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA Y METABOLISMO:\"DIETOTERAPIA, NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA Y METABOLISMO\" is a comprehensive medical text that explores the intricate relationship between diet therapy, clinical nutrition, and metabolism. This publication delves into various aspects of nutritional practices, including parenteral nutrition, and emphasizes the importance of dietary controls and their implications for health. It provides valuable insights into nutritional guidelines and practices, as well as the interactions between drugs and diet. Edited by multiple authors, including Olveira Fuster G., this work serves as an essential resource for healthcare professionals seeking to understand the role of nutrition in patient care and the impact of dietary interventions on health outcomes.", "RECOMENDACIONES DIETÉTICAS:The entity \"RECOMENDACIONES DIETÉTICAS\" refers to dietary recommendations, which are guidelines established to ensure that individuals receive the appropriate amount of nutrients and energy in their diet. These recommendations are particularly important for children, as they help to guide nutrient intake during critical growth periods. Additionally, dietary recommendations are essential for patients with chronic kidney disease, as they provide specific guidelines to maintain nutritional status and overall health. Overall, these dietary guidelines serve to promote well-being and prevent nutritional deficiencies across different populations.", "IRETON-JONES:Ireton-Jones is a researcher focused on nutritional support for cancer patients. In addition to their research, Ireton-Jones is known for developing the Ireton-Jones equation, which is utilized to estimate energy expenditure in patients, particularly those with specific medical conditions. This equation serves as a valuable tool for calculating the energy needs of critically ill patients, highlighting its importance in clinical settings.", "GASTO EN REPOSO:El gasto energético en reposo (GER) es la cantidad de energía que el cuerpo utiliza en estado de reposo para mantener funciones vitales.", "GASTO ENERGETICO TOTAL:El gasto energético total (GET) es la suma de todas las energías gastadas por un individuo en un día, incluyendo el gasto en reposo, la actividad física y la termogénesis inducida por alimentos."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}